{% render 'section-style', section: section %}
{%- comment -%}
  About.

  The About Us page body is empty on the live store — the old theme carried the
  copy in its own sections — so a template that only prints page.content shows
  nothing. This section carries the structure from the design (about.html):
  lead, origin, founder quote, the four things every glass is built from, the
  difficult part, the kitchen band, and the three "what we're not" statements.
  ("Two" was wrong here as well — the third card landed in 3e0d7d0.)

  Everything is editable. The defaults are the design's copy verbatim.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The page title was the <h1>, rendered through .non-section__title at 11px,
  while the actual statement sat in an <h2> capped at 58px. The design puts the
  statement at 88px and treats it as the page's one heading — so the eyebrow is
  an eyebrow now and the statement is the h1.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="non-about-hero">
  <div>
    <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">
      {{ section.settings.eyebrow | default: page.title }}
    </div>
    <h1 class="non-about-hero__title">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>
  </div>

  {%- if section.settings.lead != blank -%}
    <p class="non-about-hero__lead">{{ section.settings.lead }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{%- assign creds = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'credential' -%}
{%- if creds.size > 0 -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The design's credentials strip. Static rather than scrolling: four short
    facts fit on one line, and animating something nobody needs to read twice
    is motion for its own sake.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="non-creds">
    {%- for b in creds -%}
      <span class="non-creds__item" {{ b.shopify_attributes }}>{{ b.settings.text }}</span>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The wrapper is inside the test, not around it.

  This was a .non-section holding nothing but the page.content check. The About
  page keeps its copy in section settings and leaves the page body empty, so
  the div rendered with no children — and .non-section carries 48px of padding
  top and bottom, which put a 96px blank band between the credentials strip and
  The Origin. Empty on every viewport; just more obvious on a phone, where 96px
  is a fifth of the screen.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if page.content != blank -%}
  <div class="non-section">
    <div class="non-rte" style="margin-top:26px">{{ page.content }}</div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  CORRECTION. This block previously read "the design's About page carried no
  photography at all — it was type only", and the page was built on that. It is
  false: design-reference/about.html carries 19 <img> tags — six photographs,
  the founder portrait, the logotype, and six restaurant logos duplicated for
  the marquee. Everything below restores placements that were always in the
  design, rather than inventing slots.

  All six photographs are already on NON's CDN as non-story-038A8*.jpg — an
  earlier note here claimed only 038A8388 was, which came from a blocked curl
  rather than a file listing. The only asset genuinely missing is the black and
  white grade of the founder portrait; the CDN carries colour 016/019/021/022
  only, so the quote runs on colour 019 until a mono grade is uploaded.

  Each slot takes either a Shopify image picker or a CDN URL, and a slot with
  neither renders nothing rather than a broken frame.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} ── origin ────────────────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Two columns, per the design: the story on the left, one tall image on the
  right running the full height of the band. It was a single column with the
  image dropped between the body and the quote — neither the design's layout
  nor a deliberate variation on it.

  The portrait sits BESIDE the quote at 132px wide, not above it: the design
  pairs the face with the words it belongs to. The design's asset is the black
  and white headshot; the build was pointing at the colour variant.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if section.settings.origin_body != blank -%}
  {%- assign has_origin_feature = false -%}
  {%- if section.settings.origin_feature_image != blank or section.settings.origin_feature_image_url != blank -%}
    {%- assign has_origin_feature = true -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="non-about-origin{% unless has_origin_feature %} non-about-origin--solo{% endunless %}">
    <div class="non-about-origin__copy">
      <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.origin_label }}</div>
      <div class="non-step__t" style="font-size:clamp(20px,1.9vw,30px);max-width:34ch;margin-top:14px">
        {{ section.settings.origin_heading }}
      </div>
      <div class="non-rte" style="margin-top:18px">{{ section.settings.origin_body }}</div>

      {%- if section.settings.quote != blank -%}
        <figure class="non-about-quote">
          {%- if section.settings.portrait_image != blank or section.settings.portrait_image_url != blank -%}
            <div class="non-about-quote__portrait">
              {%- if section.settings.portrait_image != blank -%}
                {{ section.settings.portrait_image | image_url: width: 396, format: 'webp' | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '132,264,396', alt: section.settings.quote_cite }}
              {%- else -%}
                {% render 'cdn-image',
                   url: section.settings.portrait_image_url,
                   alt: section.settings.quote_cite,
                   sizes: '132px' %}
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
          <div>
            <blockquote class="non-press__quote" style="margin:0">
              &ldquo;{{ section.settings.quote }}&rdquo;
            </blockquote>
            <figcaption class="non-press__cite">{{ section.settings.quote_cite }}</figcaption>
          </div>
        </figure>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if has_origin_feature -%}
      <div class="non-about-origin__media">
        {%- if section.settings.origin_feature_image != blank -%}
          {{ section.settings.origin_feature_image | image_url: width: 1600, format: 'webp' | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '600,900,1200,1600', alt: section.settings.origin_feature_alt }}
        {%- else -%}
          {% render 'cdn-image',
             url: section.settings.origin_feature_image_url,
             alt: section.settings.origin_feature_alt,
             sizes: '(min-width: 860px) 50vw, 100vw' %}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} ── how it's made / what we actually do ───────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  The process rail lives INSIDE this section rather than as its own.

  It was a separate section, which meant Shopify could only order it wholly
  above or below everything here — and everything a reader thinks of as the
  middle of About (the origin story, the founder quote, what we're not) is all
  one section. There was no mid-page position to give it. Porting it in is the
  only way it can sit between the story and the what-we're-not band.

  Same classes and data attributes as before, so process-sequence.js binds to
  it unchanged.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  THE ANIMATION, not the static rail.

  This position held a five-step rail headed "What we actually do" — the same
  five steps, the same copy, drawn once and sitting still. The animation is
  that content alive: it cycles the steps, draws each fruit and botanical, and
  switches per bottle. Two versions of one idea on one page is one too many,
  and the still one was the weaker.

  Rendered INLINE rather than as its own section, for the reason the static
  rail was inlined in the first place: Shopify can only order a section wholly
  above or below this one, and everything a reader thinks of as the middle of
  About is inside here. There is no mid-page slot to give it.

  The four snippets are the artifact split to get under whatever the GitHub
  sync chokes on; Liquid concatenates their output so the HTML is identical to
  the single file. React is served from the theme, so nothing is fetched from
  unpkg — dc-support's loader short-circuits on window.React.

  The procstep and procbottle blocks are left in the schema deliberately. They
  are what the static rail read, and deleting them would drop the content from
  the theme editor with no way back if this is ever reversed.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="non-section non-process-anim" style="border-top:1px solid var(--non-line)">
  <div class="non-section__head">
    <h2 class="non-section__title">{{ section.settings.proc_heading }}</h2>
    {%- if section.settings.proc_note != blank -%}
      <span class="non-section__more">{{ section.settings.proc_note }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
  {%- if section.settings.proc_blurb != blank -%}
    <p class="non-hero__blurb" style="margin-top:16px;max-width:52ch">{{ section.settings.proc_blurb }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="non-process-anim__stage">
    {% render 'process-anim-1' %}
    {% render 'process-anim-2' %}
    {% render 'process-anim-3' %}
    {% render 'process-anim-4' %}
  </div>
</div>
<script src="{{ 'vendor-react.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'vendor-react-dom.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'dc-support.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{%- comment -%} ── the four pillars ──────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign pillars = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'pillar' -%}
{%- if pillars.size > 0 -%}
  <div class="non-section" style="border-top:1px solid var(--non-line)">
    <div class="non-section__head">
      <h2 class="non-section__title">{{ section.settings.pillars_label }}</h2>
      <span class="non-section__more">{{ section.settings.pillars_heading }}</span>
    </div>

    <div class="non-grid non-grid--4" style="margin-top:30px">
      {%- for block in pillars -%}
        <div {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <div class="non-step__n">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</div>
          {% render 'stat-icon', icon: block.settings.icon %}
          <div class="non-step__t">{{ block.settings.title }}</div>
          <p class="non-step__b">{{ block.settings.body }}</p>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} ── the difficult part ────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  This band was labelled "what we're not". It is not — that section is further
  down and renders the `not` blocks. This one is the design's "THE DIFFICULT
  PART": why water cannot carry flavour the way alcohol does, with the who and
  where facts beneath it. Mislabelled since the port; renaming the comment only,
  no markup moved.

  The design pairs it with a photograph on the left (038A8614, spicing cherries
  by hand). The slot renders nothing until an asset is set.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if section.settings.hard_video_url != blank or section.settings.hard_image != blank or section.settings.hard_image_url != blank -%}
  <div class="non-about-hard-media"{% if section.settings.hard_video_url != blank %} data-grade="{{ section.settings.hard_video_grade }}"{% endif %}>
    {%- if section.settings.hard_video_url != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Video wins over both image slots when it is set. Muted + playsinline are
        what make autoplay legal on iOS and in Chrome; without them the browser
        silently refuses to start and the band shows the poster forever.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <video
        autoplay
        muted
        loop
        playsinline
        preload="metadata"
        aria-label="{{ section.settings.hard_image_alt | escape }}"
        {% if section.settings.hard_video_poster_url != blank %}poster="{{ section.settings.hard_video_poster_url }}"{% endif %}>
        <source src="{{ section.settings.hard_video_url }}" type="video/mp4">
      </video>
      {%- if section.settings.hard_video_grain > 0 -%}
        <div class="non-about-hard-media__grain" style="opacity:{{ section.settings.hard_video_grain | divided_by: 100.0 }}"></div>
      {%- endif -%}
      <div class="non-about-hard-media__scrim"></div>
    {%- elsif section.settings.hard_image != blank -%}
      {{ section.settings.hard_image | image_url: width: 1600, format: 'webp' | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '600,900,1200,1600', alt: section.settings.hard_image_alt }}
    {%- else -%}
      {% render 'cdn-image',
         url: section.settings.hard_image_url,
         alt: section.settings.hard_image_alt,
         sizes: '(min-width: 860px) 50vw, 100vw' %}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if section.settings.hard_heading != blank -%}
  <div class="non-section non-hard">
    <div>
      <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.hard_label }}</div>
      <h2 class="non-hard__title">{{ section.settings.hard_heading }}</h2>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="non-hard__body">{{ section.settings.hard_body }}</p>

      {%- if section.settings.who_body != blank or section.settings.where_body != blank -%}
        <dl class="non-hard__facts">
          {%- if section.settings.who_body != blank -%}
            <dt class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.who_label }}</dt>
            <dd>{{ section.settings.who_body }}</dd>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.where_body != blank -%}
            <dt class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.where_label }}</dt>
            <dd>{{ section.settings.where_body }}</dd>
          {%- endif -%}
        </dl>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} ── the process rail ──────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  The six stages, from the supplied process infographic. It sits here because
  the band above it argues that every ingredient has to be handled on its own,
  and this is the evidence for that claim — the reader gets the assertion, then
  the six steps, then the photograph of the room it happens in.

  Every string is a block or a setting. The numbers are NOT: they come from
  forloop, the same way the four pillars do, so reordering stations in the theme
  editor renumbers them instead of leaving 01, 02, 02, 05 behind.

  The rail renders only when there are stations to put on it — an empty rail is
  a line across the page with nothing attached.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign stations = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'process' -%}
{%- if stations.size > 0 -%}
  <section class="non-prail">
    <div class="np-head">
      <span>{{ section.settings.process_label }}</span>
      {%- if section.settings.process_meta != blank -%}
        <span class="np-head-r">{{ section.settings.process_meta }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="np-rail">
      <div class="np-line"><div class="np-pulse"></div></div>
      <div class="np-stations">
        {%- for block in stations -%}
          <div class="np-station" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <div class="np-num">{{ forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 }}</div>
            <div class="np-dotbox"><div class="np-dot"><i></i></div></div>
            <div class="np-title">{{ block.settings.title }}</div>
            <div class="np-body">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.process_note != blank -%}
      <div class="np-foot">{{ section.settings.process_note }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </section>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} ── the kitchen band ──────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Full-bleed image with the caption sitting over it — the design's one moment of
  type on photography, at 420px tall. The caption is the page's own sentence
  ("Every ingredient is processed on its own before anything is blended"), so it
  is a setting rather than hardcoded, and the band renders only when there is an
  image to carry it. Caption over an empty frame would be worse than neither.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  THREE squares, not one full-bleed strip.

  It was a single 420px-tall band with the caption laid over it. Three square
  frames at equal size, evenly spaced, read as a set of observations from the
  same room rather than one hero shot, and squares survive a phone far better
  than a wide crop — a 2000px-wide band on a 375px screen shows a sliver of
  the middle and loses whatever the photograph was about.

  Each frame is independent, so the band renders whatever is filled in: three,
  two, or one. The caption sits BELOW the row now rather than over the
  photography — type on an image only worked because the old crop had a dead
  area to put it in.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign k1 = section.settings.kitchen_image_url_1 | default: section.settings.kitchen_image_url -%}
{%- assign has_kitchen = false -%}
{%- if section.settings.kitchen_image != blank or k1 != blank
   or section.settings.kitchen_image_url_2 != blank
   or section.settings.kitchen_image_url_3 != blank -%}
  {%- assign has_kitchen = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if has_kitchen -%}
  <figure class="non-about-kitchen">
    <div class="non-about-kitchen__grid">
      {%- if section.settings.kitchen_image != blank -%}
        <div class="non-about-kitchen__cell">
          {{ section.settings.kitchen_image | image_url: width: 900, format: 'webp'
             | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '300,600,900',
               sizes: '(min-width: 860px) 33vw, 100vw',
               class: 'non-about-kitchen__img',
               alt: section.settings.kitchen_caption }}
        </div>
      {%- elsif k1 != blank -%}
        <div class="non-about-kitchen__cell">
          {% render 'cdn-image', url: k1, alt: section.settings.kitchen_caption,
             class: 'non-about-kitchen__img', sizes: '(min-width: 860px) 33vw, 100vw' %}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.kitchen_image_2 != blank -%}
        <div class="non-about-kitchen__cell">
          {{ section.settings.kitchen_image_2 | image_url: width: 900, format: 'webp'
             | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '300,600,900',
               sizes: '(min-width: 860px) 33vw, 100vw',
               class: 'non-about-kitchen__img',
               alt: section.settings.kitchen_caption }}
        </div>
      {%- elsif section.settings.kitchen_image_url_2 != blank -%}
        <div class="non-about-kitchen__cell">
          {% render 'cdn-image', url: section.settings.kitchen_image_url_2, alt: section.settings.kitchen_caption,
             class: 'non-about-kitchen__img', sizes: '(min-width: 860px) 33vw, 100vw' %}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.kitchen_image_3 != blank -%}
        <div class="non-about-kitchen__cell">
          {{ section.settings.kitchen_image_3 | image_url: width: 900, format: 'webp'
             | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '300,600,900',
               sizes: '(min-width: 860px) 33vw, 100vw',
               class: 'non-about-kitchen__img',
               alt: section.settings.kitchen_caption }}
        </div>
      {%- elsif section.settings.kitchen_image_url_3 != blank -%}
        <div class="non-about-kitchen__cell">
          {% render 'cdn-image', url: section.settings.kitchen_image_url_3, alt: section.settings.kitchen_caption,
             class: 'non-about-kitchen__img', sizes: '(min-width: 860px) 33vw, 100vw' %}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    {%- if section.settings.kitchen_caption != blank -%}
      <figcaption class="non-about-kitchen__caption">{{ section.settings.kitchen_caption }}</figcaption>
    {%- endif -%}
  </figure>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} ── what we're not ────────────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign nots = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'not' -%}
{%- if nots.size > 0 -%}
  <div class="non-section" style="border-top:1px solid var(--non-line)">
    <div class="non-section__head">
      <h2 class="non-section__title">{{ section.settings.nots_label }}</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="non-grid" style="margin-top:26px;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr))">
      {%- for block in nots -%}
        <div {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          {%- comment -%}
            Optional picture. Renders only when one is chosen, so an empty slot
            is an empty slot rather than a grey placeholder box — and the icon
            still carries the band on its own until photography arrives.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
            <div class="non-bandimg">
              {{
                block.settings.image
                | image_url: width: 1200, format: 'webp'
                | image_tag:
                  loading: 'lazy',
                  widths: '400,700,1000,1200',
                  class: 'non-bandimg__img',
                  alt: block.settings.image_alt | default: block.settings.title
              }}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if block.settings.icon != blank and block.settings.icon != 'none' -%}
            {% render 'stat-icon', icon: block.settings.icon %}
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="non-step__t">{{ block.settings.title }}</div>
          <p class="non-step__b">{{ block.settings.body }}</p>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- assign stats = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'stat' -%}
{%- if stats.size > 0 -%}
  <div class="non-section">
    <div class="non-section__head">
      <h2 class="non-section__title">{{ section.settings.stats_label }}</h2>
      <span class="non-section__more">{{ section.settings.stats_note }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="non-stats">
      {%- for b in stats -%}
        <div class="non-stat" {{ b.shopify_attributes }}>
          {% render 'stat-icon', icon: b.settings.icon %}
          <div class="non-stat__v">{{ b.settings.value }}</div>
          <p class="non-stat__b">{{ b.settings.body }}</p>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Both CTA cards sit on photography in the design — NONHQ (038A8469) and a glass
  of NON (038A8736). The image is a block setting so each card carries its own.
  Without one the card keeps its flat panel background, which is what shipped
  until now, so an unset image degrades to the current look rather than to a
  hole. The scrim only exists when there is an image under it to darken.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign ctas = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'cta' -%}
{%- if ctas.size > 0 -%}
  <div class="non-about-ctas">
    {%- for b in ctas -%}
      {%- assign has_bg = false -%}
      {%- if b.settings.image != blank or b.settings.image_url != blank -%}
        {%- assign has_bg = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="non-about-cta{% if forloop.first and has_bg == false %} non-about-cta--solid{% endif %}{% if has_bg %} non-about-cta--media{% endif %}" {{ b.shopify_attributes }}>
        {%- if has_bg -%}
          <div class="non-about-cta__bg" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- if b.settings.image != blank -%}
              {{ b.settings.image | image_url: width: 1400, format: 'webp' | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '600,900,1400', alt: '' }}
            {%- else -%}
              {% render 'cdn-image',
                 url: b.settings.image_url,
                 alt: '',
                 sizes: '(min-width: 720px) 50vw, 100vw' %}
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="non-about-cta__inner">
          <div class="non-about-cta__title">{{ b.settings.title }}</div>
          <p class="non-about-cta__body">{{ b.settings.body }}</p>
          {%- if b.settings.label != blank -%}
            <a class="non-about-cta__link" href="{{ b.settings.url | default: '/' }}">{{ b.settings.label }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "About",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "About"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "We don't mimic wine. We make something else."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "lead",
      "label": "Lead",
      "default": "A chef-led drinks company in Melbourne, building wine alternatives out of real produce — fruit, tannin, salinity, acidity — and nothing that has ever been fermented."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Photography"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
